{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "041K", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}(f) =$", "MATH_0002": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descending-property-closed-immersion}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:365d02bf050f12ee9903b36c61bdf624d00b07c1586052591e25ad225aaf043e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6820b385da3f28ec85cbbbeab42a7dda0ecfebb097b009d680fde42aaeb5aec8", "source_text": "The property <MATH_0001>``<MATH_0002> is a closed immersion''\nis fpqc local on the base.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c2623154358789b62cdf168a1d9ae397a1191b21e7762090dee55397e01cd036", "unit_id": "tag:0420:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "041K", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nX' \\ar[r] \\ar[d] & X \\ar[d] \\\\\nZ' \\ar[r] & Z\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$Z' \\to Z$", "MATH_0004": "$X' \\to Z'$", "MATH_0005": "$X \\to Z$", "MATH_0006": "$X' \\to Z'$", "MATH_0007": "$X$", "MATH_0008": "$X \\to Z$", "MATH_0009": "$X \\to Z$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-descending-properties-morphisms}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-closed-immersion-local}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-descending-property-affine}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{descent-lemma-descending-property-closed-immersion}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:154e1bfde294518fe9236cc2bbd0a172ff18508b6a96d897faf6209a07051381", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:951c9bb3df665bc1100e01230ab701180b87e4d71f6c1fa27ce499faa63508d3", "source_text": "We will use\nLemma <REF_0001>\nto prove this. Assumptions (1) and (2) of that lemma follow from\nMorphisms of Spaces,\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nConsider a cartesian diagram\n<MATH_0001>\nof algebraic spaces over <MATH_0002>\nwhere <MATH_0003> is a surjective flat morphism of affine schemes,\nand <MATH_0004> is a closed immersion. We have to show that <MATH_0005>\nis a closed immersion. The morphism <MATH_0006> is affine. Hence by\nLemma <REF_0003>\nwe see that <MATH_0007> is a scheme and <MATH_0008> is affine.\nIt follows from\nDescent, Lemma <REF_0004>\nthat <MATH_0009> is a closed immersion as desired.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5ffd60bbee17baebeaf5d4f53a2135ba83ab481f4d7339954867854e952233f0", "unit_id": "tag:0420:proof"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "041K", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}(f) =$", "MATH_0002": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descending-property-separated}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:365d02bf050f12ee9903b36c61bdf624d00b07c1586052591e25ad225aaf043e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a220834a121d4466c3badaf5eca9daf5004e0622e29017411e9dc7b904b95f93", "source_text": "The property <MATH_0001>``<MATH_0002> is separated''\nis fpqc local on the base.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:67a2deef12a074d6e15076cc4706a83a95ac984ec456009b1830e649b6a30f42", "unit_id": "tag:0421:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "041K", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\{Y_i \\to Y\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$X_i := Y_i \\times_Y X \\to Y_i$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\Delta_i :\nX_i\n\\longrightarrow\nX_i \\times_{Y_i} X_i = Y_i \\times_Y (X \\times_Y X)\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{Y_i \\times_Y (X \\times_Y X) \\to X \\times_Y X\\}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Delta_i$", "MATH_0009": "$\\Delta : X \\to X \\times_Y X$", "MATH_0010": "$\\Delta$", "MATH_0011": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-base-change-separated}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{definition-property-morphisms-local}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{spaces-topologies-lemma-fpqc}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-descending-property-closed-immersion}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:bae9860dd5aeb53b6ae1793a09d08408beee78a4a534a0f19aefb54a1b8494a7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:043b6d4c8e79a4767e67ed0f92cb8258a1a50817169f4856bc9652cdf387f02d", "source_text": "A base change of a separated morphism is separated, see\nMorphisms of Spaces,\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nHence the direct implication in\nDefinition <REF_0002>.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nLet <MATH_0001> be an fpqc covering of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a morphism of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0004>.\nAssume each base change <MATH_0005> is separated.\nThis means that each of the morphisms\n<MATH_0006>\nis a closed immersion. The base change of a fpqc covering is an\nfpqc covering, see\nTopologies on Spaces, Lemma <REF_0003>\nhence <MATH_0007>\nis an fpqc covering of algebraic spaces. Moreover, each\n<MATH_0008> is the base change of the morphism\n<MATH_0009>. Hence it follows from\nLemma <REF_0004>\nthat <MATH_0010> is a closed immersion, i.e., <MATH_0011> is separated.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e9407e7b0680761d9a738b5faae5a1efc37b2fcf538830369fb505d385cfb94d", "unit_id": "tag:0421:proof"}
